From 7c52029c3744cf460d1a67d8264320762c7a01d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan Hertenberger <erde74@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:38:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] glenda's riostart: make the stats window first, not in
 the background

"window 0,0,161,117 ..." is the old syntax: window(1) makes such a
window from a background job (mount $wsys 'new ...' &), which can be
done after the windows below it. A new window becomes the current one,
so stats sometimes took the focus from the console window (console=0:
rc on the serial console), and the typing went to stats. With -r the
window is made at once through wctl.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/lib/dist/usr/glenda/bin/rc/riostart | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sys/lib/dist/usr/glenda/bin/rc/riostart b/sys/lib/dist/usr/glenda/bin/rc/riostart
index fde27dff3..96fe03dc0 100755
--- a/sys/lib/dist/usr/glenda/bin/rc/riostart
+++ b/sys/lib/dist/usr/glenda/bin/rc/riostart
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 #!/bin/rc
-window 0,0,161,117 stats -lmisce
+window -r 0 0 161 117 stats -lmisce
 window -miny 130
 
 # run a system shell on the serial console
-- 
